  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nonviolent Peaceforce - The NEST Project: Nonviolent Engagement for Safety and Security Transformation (2024-2031)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NEST Project (Nonviolent Engagement for Safety and Security Transformation) tackles civilian insecurity by advocating for nonviolent, community-centered security methods. NEST aims to shift from armed to community-based, nonviolent security and collective action. It challenges militarism, urging a shift to local, nonviolent strategies. Priorities include policy influence, grassroots protection leadership, and preventive actions with civilians. Engaging the UN, regional blocs, and NGOs, NEST strengthens local protection networks and promotes Unarmed Civilian Protection (UCP) understanding. Emphasis lies in transitional settings, local partnerships, and gender aspects. Activities span direct protection, training, advocacy, and engaging policymakers alongside civilians. In focus countries - DRC, Iraq, Sudan, and South Sudan - the project strengthens protection networks, gathers evidence, and implements nonviolent measures. armed actors, and mediating local peace agreements.</narrative>
  </description>
